{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L1.005","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"make","patches_required":"none"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You have a Rust project at the current directory with `Cargo.toml`. What command builds an optimised release binary? Output only the command.","ground_truth":"cargo build --release","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*cargo\\s+build\\s+(?:--release|-r)\\s*$"},"tags":["build","cargo"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L2.001","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"cmake_or_autotools","patches_required":"one_flag"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"For a CMake project using a single-config generator, configure a Release-with-debug-info build in a separate `build/` directory, then build it. Write exactly two commands: (a) configure and (b) build. Output one command per line.","ground_truth":"cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo\ncmake --build build","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A(?=[^\\r\\n]*\\bcmake\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-S\\s+\\.)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-B\\s+build)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo)[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n\\s*cmake\\s+--build\\s+build\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["build","cmake"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L2.002","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"make","patches_required":"one_flag"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Compile `prog.c` with `gcc` as a 64-bit executable named `prog`, using `-O2`, `-Wall`, and `-Werror`, and link against `libm`. Write one gcc command. Output only the command.","ground_truth":"gcc -O2 -Wall -Werror -m64 prog.c -o prog -lm","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A(?=[^\\r\\n]*\\bgcc\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-O2\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-Wall\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-Werror\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-m64\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*\\bprog\\.c\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-o\\s+prog\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*-lm\\b)[^\\r\\n]+\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":["(?:^|\\s)-m32(?:\\s|$)"],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["build","gcc"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L2.003","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"python_setup","patches_required":"zero_or_two_explicit_artifact_flags"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"To build a Python sdist AND wheel from a project with pyproject.toml without using setup.py invocation, what is the modern command (using `build`)? Output only the command.","ground_truth":"python -m build","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*(?:python|python3|py)\\s+-m\\s+build(?:\\s+(?:(?:--sdist|-s)\\s+(?:--wheel|-w)|(?:--wheel|-w)\\s+(?:--sdist|-s)))?\\s*$","case_sensitive":false},"tags":["build","pep517"],"notes":"The build frontend creates both sdist and wheel by default; explicitly requesting both via --sdist/--wheel (or -s/-w) is equivalent and accepted in either order."}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L2.004","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"cmake_or_autotools","patches_required":"one_flag"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"For a project using GNU autotools (a configure script is present), output exactly these three standard build/install steps, one command per line: configure with the explicit prefix /usr/local, build, then install using sudo. Output only the three commands.","ground_truth":"./configure --prefix=/usr/local\nmake\nsudo make install","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*\\./configure\\s+--prefix=/usr/local\\s*\\n\\s*make\\s*\\n\\s*sudo\\s+make\\s+install\\s*$","flags":[]},"tags":["build","autotools"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L2.005","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"python_setup","patches_required":"one_flag"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"You need to compile a Python C extension with custom CFLAGS='-march=native -O3' through `pip install .`. Show the single shell command (one line) that sets the env var inline and runs pip. Output only the command.","ground_truth":"CFLAGS='-march=native -O3' pip install .","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*CFLAGS=(?:'-march=native -O3'|\"-march=native -O3\")\\s+pip\\s+install\\s+\\.\\s*$","flags":[]},"tags":["build","cflags"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L3.001","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"exotic","patches_required":"source_patch"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"To build the Linux kernel for x86_64 with the default configuration and run it under QEMU, give exactly three shell commands, one per line, starting from a clean kernel source tree: (1) generate the default configuration; (2) build the bzImage using all available CPU cores; (3) start qemu-system-x86_64 with the produced bzImage passed via -kernel and with -nographic. Output only the three commands.","ground_truth":"make defconfig\nmake -j$(nproc) bzImage\nqemu-system-x86_64 -kernel arch/x86/boot/bzImage -nographic","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\Amake\\s+defconfig\\r?\\nmake\\s+-j(?:\\$\\(nproc\\)|\\\"\\$\\(nproc\\)\\\"|\\$\\(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN\\)|\\\"\\$\\(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN\\)\\\")\\s+bzImage\\r?\\nqemu-system-x86_64\\s+-kernel\\s+\\.?/?arch/x86/boot/bzImage\\s+-nographic\\Z"},"tags":["build","kernel","qemu"]}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L3.002","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"exotic","patches_required":"source_patch"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"To bootstrap SQLite from an unpacked SQLite autoconf source tarball (a source tree containing ./configure) with gcov coverage instrumentation enabled, output exactly two shell commands, one per line: first configure the tree with CFLAGS containing -fprofile-arcs, -ftest-coverage, and -O0, LDFLAGS containing -lgcov, and --enable-debug; then run make. Output only the commands.","ground_truth":"./configure CFLAGS='-fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage -O0' LDFLAGS='-lgcov' --enable-debug\nmake","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A(?=[^\\r\\n]*\\./configure\\b)(?=[^\\r\\n]*--enable-debug\\b)[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n\\s*make\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"required_literal_patterns":["CFLAGS\\s*=\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*-fprofile-arcs[^'\\\"]*-ftest-coverage[^'\\\"]*-O0[^'\\\"]*['\\\"]","LDFLAGS\\s*=\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*-lgcov[^'\\\"]*['\\\"]"]}},"tags":["build","sqlite","gcov"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L3.003","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"exotic","patches_required":"source_patch"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Assume a POSIX shell and that `setup.py` already defines an Extension whose `extra_compile_args` and `extra_link_args` are appended in compiler/linker-valid positions. Write exactly one command line to build it in place, adding `/opt/foo/include` to the C compiler include path and `/opt/foo/lib` plus `libfoo` to the linker inputs. Use `python setup.py build_ext --inplace`; output only the command line.","ground_truth":"CFLAGS='-I/opt/foo/include' LDFLAGS='-L/opt/foo/lib -lfoo' python setup.py build_ext --inplace","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":false,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["\\A\\s*(?:CFLAGS=['\\\"]-I/opt/foo/include['\\\"]\\s+LDFLAGS=['\\\"]-L/opt/foo/lib\\s+-lfoo['\\\"]\\s+python\\s+setup\\.py\\s+build_ext\\s+--inplace|python\\s+setup\\.py\\s+build_ext\\s+--inplace\\s+(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:-I/opt/foo/include|--include-dirs=/opt/foo/include))(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:-L/opt/foo/lib|--library-dirs=/opt/foo/lib))(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:-lfoo|--libraries=foo))[^\\r\\n]*)\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"source_language":"shell"}},"tags":["build","cython"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L3.004","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"exotic","patches_required":"source_patch"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Assume you are running the command from the workspace root. Its `Cargo.toml` contains both a `[workspace]` section and a `[package]` section for the root crate, and `Cargo.lock` is in the same directory. Using Cargo 1.62+, add `aho-corasick` with the version requirement `\"1\"` to the root crate and update the lockfile. Output only one cargo command.","ground_truth":"cargo add aho-corasick@1","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"shell","checks":{"commands":["cargo"],"tokens":["add","aho-corasick@1"]}},"tags":["build","cargo","add"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.build_system_use.L3.005","canonical_id":"code.build_system_use","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"system_familiarity":"exotic","patches_required":"source_patch"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"To configure a CMake project for cross-compilation to aarch64 from an x86_64 host, output exactly one CMake configure command. The toolchain file `aarch64-linux.cmake` is at the project root. Use `build` as the build directory and configure a Release build.","ground_truth":"cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=aarch64-linux.cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:^|\\s)-S\\s+\\.(?:\\s|$))(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:^|\\s)-B\\s+build(?:\\s|$))(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:^|\\s)(?:-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE(?::FILEPATH)?=aarch64-linux\\.cmake|--toolchain\\s+aarch64-linux\\.cmake)(?:\\s|$))(?=[^\\r\\n]*(?:^|\\s)-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE(?::STRING)?=Release(?:\\s|$))cmake(?:\\s+[^\\r\\n]+)*\\Z"},"tags":["build","cross","cmake"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L1.001","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"language":"cython","interaction":"self_contained"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Edit this Cython function so it adds 2 instead of 1; do not introduce any C-API calls. Original:\n```\ndef add_one(int x):\n    return x + 1\n```\nOutput only the corrected Cython function definition.","ground_truth":"def add_one(int x):\n    return x + 2","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A\\s*def\\s+add_one\\s*\\(\\s*int\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)\\s*:\\s*\\n\\s*return\\s+\\1\\s*\\+\\s*2\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":["\\bPy[A-Z_]\\w*\\s*\\("],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["native","cython"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L1.002","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"language":"cython","interaction":"self_contained"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"In the following Cython function, add a `cdef int i` declaration for the loop variable so that Cython can use a C integer loop index. Make no other semantic changes. Output only the corrected function.\n```\ndef sum_n(int n):\n    s = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        s += i\n    return s\n```","ground_truth":"def sum_n(int n):\n    cdef int i\n    s = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        s += i\n    return s","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A\\s*def\\s+sum_n\\s*\\(\\s*int\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)\\s*:[\\s\\S]*\\bcdef\\s+int\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)[\\s\\S]*\\bfor\\s+\\2\\s+in\\s+range\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*\\)\\s*:[\\s\\S]*\\bs\\s*\\+=\\s*\\2[\\s\\S]*return\\s+s\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["native","cython","cdef"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L1.003","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"language":"cython","interaction":"self_contained"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Convert the following Python-style Cython function so that `s` is declared as a typed `cdef double` accumulator. Preserve the behavior. The loop variable does not need to be explicitly typed. Original:\n```\ndef mean(int n):\n    s = 0.0\n    for i in range(n): s += i\n    return s / n\n```\nOutput only the corrected Cython function.","ground_truth":"def mean(int n):\n    cdef double s = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        s += i\n    return s / n","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\A\\s*def\\s+mean\\s*\\(\\s*int\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)\\s*:[\\s\\S]*\\bcdef\\s+double\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*=\\s*0\\.0[\\s\\S]*\\bfor\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s+in\\s+range\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*\\2\\s*\\+=\\s*\\3[\\s\\S]*return\\s+\\2\\s*/\\s*\\1\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["native","cython"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L1.004","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"language":"cython","interaction":"self_contained"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"In Cython, define a `cdef inline` function `_sq(double x)` that returns `x * x` using C `double` values, with no Python-call overhead when called from Cython. Output only the function definition.","ground_truth":"cdef inline double _sq(double x):\n    return x * x","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"\\A(?:\\s*cdef\\s+inline\\s+double\\s+_sq\\s*\\(\\s*double\\s+x\\s*\\)\\s*:\\s*\\n\\s+return\\s+\\(?\\s*x\\s*\\*\\s*x\\s*\\)?\\s*)\\Z","flags":[]},"tags":["native","cython","inline"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L1.005","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L1","axis_values":{"language":"cython","interaction":"self_contained"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Modify this Cython function by decorating the function to disable bounds checking and negative-index wraparound for the indexed access in the loop. Keep the function's behavior unchanged. Output only the corrected Cython code; include the required cython import/cimport if needed.\n```\ndef sum_arr(double[:] xs):\n    s = 0.0\n    for i in range(xs.shape[0]):\n        s += xs[i]\n    return s\n```","ground_truth":"cimport cython\n\n@cython.boundscheck(False)\n@cython.wraparound(False)\ndef sum_arr(double[:] xs):\n    s = 0.0\n    for i in range(xs.shape[0]):\n        s += xs[i]\n    return s","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"shell","required_patterns":["\\bcimport\\s+cython\\b","@cython\\.boundscheck\\s*\\(\\s*False\\s*\\)","@cython\\.wraparound\\s*\\(\\s*False\\s*\\)","def\\s+sum_arr\\s*\\(\\s*double\\s*\\[:\\]\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)\\s*:[\\s\\S]*for\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s+in\\s+range\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\.shape\\s*\\[\\s*0\\s*\\]\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*\\bs\\s*\\+=\\s*\\1\\s*\\[\\s*\\2\\s*\\][\\s\\S]*return\\s+s\\s*\\Z"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["native","cython","perf"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L2.001","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"calls_back_into_python"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a complete CPython C extension function definition and a PyMethodDef array entry. The exported function must accept exactly one Python int (including arbitrarily large Python integers) and return its exact square as a new Python int using the standard CPython C-API. Reject non-int arguments with the normal CPython exception behavior. Output only the C source for the function definition and PyMethodDef array.","ground_truth":"static PyObject* py_square(PyObject* self, PyObject* args) {\n    PyObject *x;\n    if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args, \"O!:square\", &PyLong_Type, &x)) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    return PyNumber_Multiply(x, x);\n}\n\nstatic PyMethodDef Methods[] = {\n    {\"square\", py_square, METH_VARARGS, \"Square an int.\"},\n    {NULL, NULL, 0, NULL}\n};","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["static\\s+PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*\\(\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*self\\s*,\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*args\\s*\\)","PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\(\\s*args\\s*,\\s*['\\\"]O!(?::square)?['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*&PyLong_Type\\s*,\\s*&\\w+\\s*\\)","(?:return\\s+PyNumber_Multiply\\s*\\(\\s*(\\w+)\\s*,\\s*\\1\\s*\\)|(?:\\w+\\s*=\\s*PyNumber_Multiply\\s*\\(\\s*(\\w+)\\s*,\\s*\\2\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*return\\s+\\w+\\s*;))","PyMethodDef","['\\\"]square['\\\"][\\s\\S]*METH_VARARGS"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"source_language":"c"}},"tags":["native","c","capi"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L2.002","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"calls_back_into_python"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"In CPython C extension code, write a complete definition of `static PyObject *py_callme(PyObject *self, PyObject *args)`. It must accept exactly one positional argument, verify that it is callable, raise `TypeError` if it is not callable, and invoke it with zero positional and keyword arguments. Return the callable's result, propagating any exception. Use correct CPython reference ownership; do not add unnecessary INCREF/DECREF operations. You may use `PyObject_CallObject(fn, NULL)` or another equivalent zero-argument call API.","ground_truth":"static PyObject *py_callme(PyObject *self, PyObject *args)\n{\n    PyObject *fn;\n\n    if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args, \"O\", &fn)) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    if (!PyCallable_Check(fn)) {\n        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError, \"argument must be callable\");\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    return PyObject_CallObject(fn, NULL);\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["\\bpy_callme\\s*\\(","PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\([^;]*['\\\"]O(?::callme)?['\\\"]","PyCallable_Check\\s*\\(","PyErr_SetString\\s*\\(\\s*PyExc_TypeError","return\\s+(?:PyObject_CallObject\\s*\\(\\s*\\w+\\s*,\\s*NULL\\s*\\)|PyObject_CallNoArgs\\s*\\(\\s*\\w+\\s*\\))"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":["\\bPy_(?:INCREF|DECREF)\\s*\\("],"pattern_counts":{},"source_language":"c"}},"tags":["native","c","callback"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L2.003","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"calls_back_into_python"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a complete CPython C extension function definition `static PyObject* py_sum_list(PyObject* self, PyObject* args)`. It must accept exactly one Python list, validate it with PyList_Check, obtain its length with PyList_Size, and retrieve elements with PyList_GetItem without DECREFing the borrowed references. Each element must be converted with PyLong_AsLong, checking `v == -1 && PyErr_Occurred()`. Return the sum as a Python int. If an element cannot fit in C long, propagate the PyLong_AsLong error. If the accumulated C long sum would overflow, raise OverflowError. Output only the complete function definition.","ground_truth":"static PyObject* py_sum_list(PyObject* self, PyObject* args) {\n    PyObject* lst;\n    if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args, \"O\", &lst)) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    if (!PyList_Check(lst)) {\n        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError, \"expected a list\");\n        return NULL;\n    }\n\n    Py_ssize_t n = PyList_Size(lst);\n    if (n < 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n\n    long total = 0;\n    for (Py_ssize_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        PyObject* item = PyList_GetItem(lst, i);\n        if (item == NULL) {\n            return NULL;\n        }\n\n        long v = PyLong_AsLong(item);\n        if (v == -1 && PyErr_Occurred()) {\n            return NULL;\n        }\n        if ((v > 0 && total > LONG_MAX - v) ||\n            (v < 0 && total < LONG_MIN - v)) {\n            PyErr_SetString(PyExc_OverflowError, \"sum does not fit in C long\");\n            return NULL;\n        }\n        total += v;\n    }\n\n    return PyLong_FromLong(total);\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"c","required_patterns":["static\\s+PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*py_sum_list\\s*\\(\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*,\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*\\)","PyList_Check\\s*\\(","PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*=\\s*PyList_GetItem\\s*\\(","LONG_MAX\\s*-","LONG_MIN\\s*-","return\\s+PyLong_FromLong\\s*\\("],"required_any_patterns":[["Py_ssize_t\\s+\\w+\\s*=\\s*PyList_Size\\s*\\(","Py_ssize_t\\s+[^;]+;[\\s\\S]*\\b[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\s*=\\s*PyList_Size\\s*\\("],["long\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*=\\s*PyLong_AsLong\\s*\\([^)]+\\)[\\s\\S]*if\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*==\\s*-1\\s*&&\\s*PyErr_Occurred\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\)","long\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*;[\\s\\S]*\\b\\1\\s*=\\s*PyLong_AsLong\\s*\\([^)]+\\)[\\s\\S]*if\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*==\\s*-1\\s*&&\\s*PyErr_Occurred\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\)"]],"forbidden_patterns":["Py_(?:DECREF|XDECREF)\\s*\\("],"pattern_counts":{},"required_literal_patterns":["PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\([^,]+,\\s*['\\\"]O(?::[A-Za-z_]\\w*)?['\\\"]\\s*,"]}},"tags":["native","c","list"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L2.004","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"calls_back_into_python"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Add a C extension function `py_repeat(s, n)` and one `PyMethodDef` entry exposing it as `repeat`. Parse `s` as an exact Unicode object and `n` as `Py_ssize_t`. Obtain UTF-8 bytes with `PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize`, repeat those bytes, and create the result with `PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize`. Define negative `n` as producing an empty string. Before multiplication or allocation, reject an unrepresentable total byte length with `OverflowError`; propagate all other Python/C-API errors correctly. Output only C source.","ground_truth":"static PyObject *\npy_repeat(PyObject *self, PyObject *args)\n{\n    PyObject *s;\n    Py_ssize_t n, len, total;\n    const char *buf;\n    char *out;\n    PyObject *res;\n\n    if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args, \"Un\", &s, &n))\n        return NULL;\n\n    buf = PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize(s, &len);\n    if (buf == NULL)\n        return NULL;\n\n    if (n <= 0 || len == 0)\n        return PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize(\"\", 0);\n\n    if (len > PY_SSIZE_T_MAX / n) {\n        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_OverflowError, \"repeated string is too large\");\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    total = len * n;\n\n    out = PyMem_Malloc((size_t)total);\n    if (out == NULL)\n        return PyErr_NoMemory();\n\n    for (Py_ssize_t i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        memcpy(out + i * len, buf, (size_t)len);\n\n    res = PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize(out, total);\n    PyMem_Free(out);\n    return res;\n}\n\nstatic PyMethodDef RepMethods[] = {\n    {\"repeat\", py_repeat, METH_VARARGS, \"Repeat string.\"},\n    {NULL, NULL, 0, NULL}\n};","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"c","required_patterns":["static\\s+PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*py_repeat\\s*\\(","PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize\\s*\\(","if\\s*\\([^)]*[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\s*<\\s*=?\\s*0[^)]*\\)[\\s\\S]*PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize\\s*\\(","PY_SSIZE_T_MAX\\s*/","PyExc_OverflowError","PyMem_Malloc\\s*\\(","PyErr_NoMemory\\s*\\(","memcpy\\s*\\(","PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize\\s*\\(","PyMem_Free\\s*\\(","PyMethodDef[\\s\\S]*METH_VARARGS"],"required_any_patterns":[["if\\s*\\([^)]*[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\s*<=\\s*0[^)]*\\)[\\s\\S]*PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize\\s*\\(","if\\s*\\([^)]*[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\s*==\\s*0[^)]*\\)[\\s\\S]*PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize\\s*\\("]],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"required_literal_patterns":["\\{\\s*['\\\"]repeat['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*py_repeat\\s*,\\s*METH_VARARGS"],"required_any_literal_patterns":[["PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\([^,]+,\\s*['\\\"]Un['\\\"]\\s*,","PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\([^,]+,\\s*['\\\"]On(?::repeat)?['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*&([A-Za-z_]\\w*)[\\s\\S]*PyUnicode_CheckExact\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*\\)"]]}},"tags":["native","c","unicode"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L2.005","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"calls_back_into_python"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Assume `say_hi` is already defined with a CPython-compatible `METH_VARARGS` signature. Write the C source for a Python 3 CPython extension module named `mymod` that exposes exactly one module-level function named `say_hi`. Output only the `PyMethodDef` table, the `PyModuleDef`, and `PyInit_mymod`.","ground_truth":"static PyMethodDef mymod_methods[] = {\n    {\"say_hi\", say_hi, METH_VARARGS, NULL},\n    {NULL, NULL, 0, NULL}\n};\n\nstatic struct PyModuleDef mymod_module = {\n    PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT,\n    \"mymod\",\n    NULL,\n    -1,\n    mymod_methods\n};\n\nPyMODINIT_FUNC PyInit_mymod(void) {\n    return PyModule_Create(&mymod_module);\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"c","required_patterns":["static\\s+PyMethodDef\\s+[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\s*\\[\\s*\\]\\s*=\\s*\\{[\\s\\S]*\\{\\s*NULL\\s*,\\s*NULL\\s*,\\s*0\\s*,\\s*NULL\\s*\\}","static\\s+struct\\s+PyModuleDef\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*=\\s*\\{[\\s\\S]*PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT[\\s\\S]*-1[\\s\\S]*\\}\\s*;?[\\s\\S]*PyMODINIT_FUNC\\s+PyInit_mymod\\s*\\(\\s*void\\s*\\)\\s*\\{\\s*return\\s+PyModule_Create\\s*\\(\\s*&\\1\\s*\\)\\s*;\\s*\\}"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{"\\bMETH_VARARGS\\b":1},"required_literal_patterns":["\\{\\s*['\\\"]say_hi['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*say_hi\\s*,\\s*METH_VARARGS","PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT[\\s\\S]*['\\\"]mymod['\\\"]"]}},"tags":["native","c","module_init"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L3.001","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"language":"cpp_or_rust","interaction":"shares_state_with_caller"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write Rust code using PyO3 0.21 that exposes a Python-callable function `add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64`. Include a `#[pymodule]` initialization function named `pyrust` that registers `add` in the module. Output only Rust code.","ground_truth":"use pyo3::prelude::*;\n\n#[pyfunction]\nfn add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 { a + b }\n\n#[pymodule]\nfn pyrust(m: &Bound<'_, PyModule>) -> PyResult<()> {\n    m.add_function(wrap_pyfunction!(add, m)?)?;\n    Ok(())\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"rust","required_patterns":["\\buse\\s+pyo3::prelude::\\*\\s*;","#\\s*\\[\\s*pyfunction\\s*\\]","fn\\s+add\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*:\\s*i64\\s*,\\s*([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*:\\s*i64\\s*\\)\\s*->\\s*i64\\s*\\{\\s*\\1\\s*\\+\\s*\\2\\s*\\}","#\\s*\\[\\s*pymodule\\s*\\][\\s\\S]*fn\\s+pyrust\\s*\\([\\s\\S]*PyModule[\\s\\S]*\\)[\\s\\S]*wrap_pyfunction!\\s*\\(\\s*add\\s*,[\\s\\S]*\\)[\\s\\S]*Ok\\s*\\(\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\)"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{}}},"tags":["native","rust","pyo3"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L3.002","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"language":"cpp_or_rust"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a pybind11 C++ binding that exposes a class `Counter` with methods inc() (no-arg) and value() (returns int) plus a constructor taking int start. Module name is `cppbind`. Output only the C++ source.","ground_truth":"#include <pybind11/pybind11.h>\nnamespace py = pybind11;\n\nclass Counter {\npublic:\n    int v;\n    Counter(int start) : v(start) {}\n    void inc() { v++; }\n    int value() const { return v; }\n};\n\nPYBIND11_MODULE(cppbind, m) {\n    py::class_<Counter>(m, \"Counter\")\n        .def(py::init<int>())\n        .def(\"inc\", &Counter::inc)\n        .def(\"value\", &Counter::value);\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"c_like","required_patterns":["#include\\s*<pybind11/pybind11\\.h>","class\\s+Counter\\s*\\{","(?:explicit\\s+)?Counter\\s*\\(\\s*int\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*:\\s*([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*void\\s+inc\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\{[^{}]*(?:\\+\\+\\s*\\2\\b|\\b\\2\\s*(?:\\+\\+|\\+=\\s*1))[^{}]*\\}[\\s\\S]*int\\s+value\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*const\\s*\\{\\s*return\\s+\\2\\s*;","PYBIND11_MODULE\\s*\\(\\s*cppbind\\s*,\\s*([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*py::class_<\\s*Counter\\s*>\\s*\\(\\s*\\1","\\.def\\s*\\(\\s*['\\\"]inc['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*&Counter::inc\\s*\\)","\\.def\\s*\\(\\s*['\\\"]value['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*&Counter::value\\s*\\)"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"required_literal_patterns":["py::class_<\\s*Counter\\s*>\\s*\\([^,]+,\\s*['\\\"]Counter['\\\"]"]}},"tags":["native","cpp","pybind11"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L3.003","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"language":"cpp_or_rust","interaction":"shares_state_with_caller"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Using NumPy's modern ArrayMethod indexed-loop ABI, write only the C function definition for `minimum_indexed_int64` with this exact signature:\n\n`static int minimum_indexed_int64(PyArrayMethod_Context *NPY_UNUSED(context), char *const *args, npy_intp const *dimensions, npy_intp const *steps, NpyAuxData *NPY_UNUSED(aux))`\n\nImplement the indexed loop used by `np.minimum.at` for int64 data. `args[0]` is the base byte pointer of the destination int64 array, `args[1]` is a sequence of `npy_intp` indices, and `args[2]` is a sequence of int64 values. `dimensions[0]` is the number of updates. `steps[0]` is the destination array byte stride used with each index, while `steps[1]` and `steps[2]` are the byte strides for indices and values. For each update, write the value to the indexed destination only when the new value is smaller. Return 0.","ground_truth":"static int\nminimum_indexed_int64(PyArrayMethod_Context *NPY_UNUSED(context),\n                     char *const *args, npy_intp const *dimensions,\n                     npy_intp const *steps, NpyAuxData *NPY_UNUSED(aux))\n{\n    char *iarr = args[0];\n    char *indx = args[1];\n    char *value = args[2];\n    npy_intp is1 = steps[0], is2 = steps[1], is3 = steps[2];\n    npy_intp n = dimensions[0];\n\n    for (npy_intp i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        npy_intp idx = *(npy_intp *)indx;\n        npy_int64 *dst = (npy_int64 *)(iarr + idx * is1);\n        npy_int64 v = *(npy_int64 *)value;\n        if (v < *dst) {\n            *dst = v;\n        }\n        indx += is2;\n        value += is3;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"required_patterns":["minimum_indexed_int64\\s*\\(","char\\s*\\*\\s*const\\s*\\*\\s*args","args\\s*\\[\\s*0\\s*\\]","args\\s*\\[\\s*1\\s*\\]","args\\s*\\[\\s*2\\s*\\]","steps\\s*\\[\\s*0\\s*\\]","steps\\s*\\[\\s*1\\s*\\]","steps\\s*\\[\\s*2\\s*\\]","(?:npy_int64|int64_t)\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+","if\\s*\\([^)]*<\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*\\)","return\\s+0\\s*;"],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"source_language":"c"}},"tags":["native","c","numpy_ufunc"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L3.004","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"language":"cpp_or_rust","interaction":"shares_state_with_caller"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"In a Rust crate's Cargo.toml, you need to add the `aho-corasick` v1 dependency AND ensure features=['std'] is enabled. Output exactly two TOML lines: first the literal section header `[dependencies]`, then the `aho-corasick` dependency entry. Output no other lines or prose.","ground_truth":"[dependencies]\naho-corasick = { version = \"1\", features = [\"std\"] }","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"toml","checks":{"path_equals":{"dependencies.aho-corasick.version":"1","dependencies.aho-corasick.features":["std"]}}},"tags":["native","rust","cargo"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"code.native_module_edit.L3.005","canonical_id":"code.native_module_edit","category":"code","level":"L3","axis_values":{"language":"c","interaction":"shares_state_with_caller"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a complete CPython C extension function `static PyObject* py_set_attr(PyObject* self, PyObject* args)` that parses `(obj, name, value)`, where `name` is a C string, sets attribute `name` on `obj` to `value` using `PyObject_SetAttrString`, returns NULL if parsing or attribute setting fails, and otherwise returns a new reference to `Py_None`. Use explicit `Py_INCREF(Py_None); return Py_None;`. Output only the complete function definition.","ground_truth":"static PyObject* py_set_attr(PyObject* self, PyObject* args) {\n    PyObject* obj;\n    const char* name;\n    PyObject* value;\n    if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args, \"OsO\", &obj, &name, &value)) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    if (PyObject_SetAttrString(obj, name, value) < 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    Py_INCREF(Py_None);\n    return Py_None;\n}","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"source_contract","checks":{"balanced_delimiters":true,"case_sensitive":true,"source_language":"c","required_patterns":[],"required_any_patterns":[],"forbidden_patterns":[],"pattern_counts":{},"required_literal_patterns":["static\\s+PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*py_set_attr\\s*\\(\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\w+\\s*,\\s*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\)\\s*\\{(?=[\\s\\S]*PyArg_ParseTuple\\s*\\(\\s*\\1\\s*,\\s*['\\\"]OsO['\\\"]\\s*,\\s*&([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*,\\s*&([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*,\\s*&([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\\s*\\))(?=[\\s\\S]*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\2\\b)(?=[\\s\\S]*const\\s+char\\s*\\*\\s*\\3\\b)(?=[\\s\\S]*PyObject\\s*\\*\\s*\\4\\b)(?=[\\s\\S]*PyObject_SetAttrString\\s*\\(\\s*\\2\\s*,\\s*\\3\\s*,\\s*\\4\\s*\\)\\s*(?:<\\s*0|==\\s*-1))(?=[\\s\\S]*return\\s+NULL)(?=[\\s\\S]*Py_INCREF\\s*\\(\\s*Py_None\\s*\\)\\s*;\\s*return\\s+Py_None\\s*;)[\\s\\S]*\\}"]}},"tags":["native","c","refcount"]}
