{"probe_id":"code.complexity_analysis.L2.004","canonical_id":"code.complexity_analysis","category":"code","level":"L2","axis_values":{"task":"judge_optimal","algorithm_distance":"different_class"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"For single-source shortest paths in a directed graph with non-negative edge weights, what is the worst-case time complexity of Dijkstra's algorithm when the graph is stored with adjacency lists and the priority queue is a binary min-heap? Use V for vertices and E for edges. Reply with exactly one of: O(V+E), O((V+E) log V), O(V^2), O(V*E).","ground_truth":"O((V+E) log V)","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"O((V+E) log V)","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["complexity","graph"],"notes":""}
